<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masfut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masfut is an inland exclave of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of Ajman in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajar-mountains">Hajar Mountains</a> of the United Arab Emirates, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and the Dubai enclave of Hatta. A small farming town of date gardens and falaj irrigation, it is one of two detached territories, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manama">Manama</a>, that Ajman holds far from its coastal capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masfut.jpg" alt="Masfut" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: IbrahimKumar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masfut_and_Hatta_-_Panoramic_view_from_Al_Bomah_Tower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
